 Reads vendor order exports (CSV), normalizes the columns, drops duplicate orders and posts the rows to the warehouse HTTP API at `WAREHOUSE_URL`.
 
 The loader streams CSV rows and posts batches of at most 2,000 rows.
+Uploads split further as needed to keep each encoded JSON request at or below
+the warehouse's 4,000,000-byte limit. A single row that exceeds this limit raises
+`ValueError`; earlier requests may already have been uploaded.
 Timestamp normalization uses a per-file cache of at most 4,096 values to speed up
 exports with repeated timestamps without retaining all timestamps in memory.
 Deduplication keeps the first occurrence across the entire file; its set of order keys grows with the number of unique orders.
